From: qualixxe <qualixxe@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dpu: do not split a single-slice DSC panel over two blocks

dpu_encoder_update_topology() always reserves two DSC blocks (and, via
dpu_crtc_get_topology(), two layer mixers) whenever the catalog has two DSC
blocks, regardless of what the panel asked for. dpu_encoder_prep_dsc() then
feeds each block intf_ip_w / num_dsc pixels while dpu_hw_dsc_config() writes
dsc->slice_width into DSC_SLICE verbatim, so a panel that declares one slice
covering the whole line gets two encoders each programming a full-width slice
over half a line.

courbet's K9A panel is exactly that case: its downstream dtsi and the dtbo
dumped from the phone both declare slice-width 1080, slice-per-pkt 1 and
qcom,display-topology = <1 1 1>. The panel decoder is initialised for one
1080-wide slice per line, so the DPU must use one DSC block and one LM.

Respect slice_count when it is 1. dpu_crtc_get_topology() then picks num_lm
from hdisplay (1080 is not > MAX_HDISPLAY_SPLIT), giving the 1:1:1 topology
the panel expects. Panels that declare two slices per line keep the existing
2 DSC / 2 LM behaviour.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder.c
@@ -684,10 +684,17 @@
 		 * screens.
 		 */
 		WARN(topology->num_intf > 2,
 		     "DSC topology cannot support more than 2 interfaces\n");
-		if (topology->num_intf >= 2 || dpu_kms->catalog->dsc_count >= 2)
+		/*
+		 * One slice per line means one DSC encoder: splitting the line
+		 * would change the slice geometry the panel decoder was
+		 * programmed with.
+		 */
+		if (dsc->slice_count == 1)
+			topology->num_dsc = 1;
+		else if (topology->num_intf >= 2 || dpu_kms->catalog->dsc_count >= 2)
 			topology->num_dsc = 2;
 		else
 			topology->num_dsc = 1;
 	}
 
